WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.800
Why does this module exist?

2
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:02.925
Here's the story.

3
00:00:02.925 --> 00:00:06.509
Entra inbound provisioning
writes department from HR.

4
00:00:06.509 --> 00:00:09.938
SailPoint's Entra connector
also writes department.

5
00:00:09.938 --> 00:00:11.988
Each sync overwrites the other.

6
00:00:11.988 --> 00:00:15.632
And the drift you'll measure in
Module 4 comes back the next day,

7
00:00:15.632 --> 00:00:17.775
no matter how often someone fixes it.

8
00:00:17.775 --> 00:00:20.254
The reconciliation sees the result,

9
00:00:20.254 --> 00:00:24.137
attribute drift that keeps
coming back, but not the cause.

10
00:00:24.137 --> 00:00:26.810
Fixing the value by hand never settles it,

11
00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.562
because the next sync recreates the drift.

12
00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:33.145
Gate 2 settles it on paper,
before anything is connected:

13
00:00:33.145 --> 00:00:37.662
one writer per attribute, and one
approver system per authority class.

14
00:00:37.662 --> 00:00:39.950
In this module you learn those decisions,

15
00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:43.920
and you check two provisioning
configurations against the first one.
